00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:31,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:39,477
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:10,068
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

3
00:02:10,652 --> 00:02:12,445
‎EPISODE 7

4
00:02:22,914 --> 00:02:23,748
‎May I come in?

5
00:02:23,831 --> 00:02:25,124
‎I'm sorry, sir.

6
00:02:25,208 --> 00:02:28,169
‎But this area is off-limits.

7
00:02:28,253 --> 00:02:30,213
‎No unauthorized access.

8
00:02:30,296 --> 00:02:33,383
‎I need to speak with the conductor
‎who performed last.

9
00:02:33,466 --> 00:02:34,509
‎His name is…

10
00:02:35,134 --> 00:02:36,344
‎Luca Domenico.

11
00:02:36,427 --> 00:02:38,763
‎But the competition is still in progress.

12
00:02:38,846 --> 00:02:40,974
‎Outside contact is not permitted.

13
00:02:45,603 --> 00:02:46,437
‎Okay.

14
00:03:02,286 --> 00:03:03,496
‎Choi Jeong-yo!

15
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:04,998
‎Choi Jeong-yo!

16
00:03:13,715 --> 00:03:14,590
‎It's Jeong-yo.

17
00:03:15,675 --> 00:03:16,718
‎It's definitely him.

18
00:03:18,136 --> 00:03:19,887
‎I'd recognize you anywhere.

19
00:03:39,157 --> 00:03:40,116
‎Yes, Mr. Kang?

20
00:03:40,616 --> 00:03:42,410
‎It's late. Is everything okay?

21
00:03:42,493 --> 00:03:44,495
‎Go online right now

22
00:03:45,121 --> 00:03:48,166
‎and watch the video
‎of the conducting competition in Brno.

23
00:03:49,042 --> 00:03:52,045
‎Oh, right. Today was the final round.

24
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:53,963
‎But why?

25
00:03:54,047 --> 00:03:56,174
‎Did you find someone you like?

26
00:03:56,758 --> 00:03:58,509
‎Choi Jeong-yo has returned.

27
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,136
‎Who?

28
00:04:00,219 --> 00:04:01,763
‎Choi Jeong-yo.

29
00:04:01,846 --> 00:04:03,473
‎The one who disappeared nine years ago.

30
00:04:04,182 --> 00:04:05,058
‎Don't you remember him?

31
00:04:09,979 --> 00:04:11,481
‎Hello, this is Pi-o Kang.

32
00:04:12,231 --> 00:04:13,483
‎Do you know where Jeong-yo is…

33
00:04:13,983 --> 00:04:16,819
‎I mean, Luca Domenico is staying?

34
00:04:36,130 --> 00:04:38,091
‎I'm here to meet Luca Domenico.

35
00:04:39,884 --> 00:04:41,886
‎I'm sorry, but you'll have to leave.

36
00:04:41,969 --> 00:04:45,223
‎We've been instructed not to allow
‎any contact with the press.

37
00:04:47,809 --> 00:04:49,727
‎I'm not the press. Just a friend.

38
00:04:51,521 --> 00:04:52,563
‎Well…

39
00:04:54,565 --> 00:04:57,193
‎It's quite late, and he's likely asleep.

40
00:04:57,276 --> 00:04:58,861
‎Tell him Pi-o Kang is here.

41
00:04:59,362 --> 00:05:00,530
‎He will see me.

42
00:05:01,864 --> 00:05:03,032
‎Please wait one moment.

43
00:05:08,121 --> 00:05:09,330
‎Hello, Mr. Domenico?

44
00:05:09,914 --> 00:05:11,416
‎I'm so sorry to bother you,

45
00:05:11,499 --> 00:05:15,169
‎but there's someone here
‎who says he's your friend

46
00:05:15,253 --> 00:05:17,004
‎and that he would like to see you.

47
00:05:17,088 --> 00:05:18,548
‎It's Pi-o Kang.

48
00:05:24,262 --> 00:05:26,973
‎I'm sorry, but Mr. Domenico says
‎he doesn't know you.

49
00:05:28,599 --> 00:05:30,143
‎He said he doesn't know me?

50
00:05:30,226 --> 00:05:32,311
‎Yes, I'm sorry.

51
00:05:36,566 --> 00:05:37,859
‎Is there anything else
‎I can help you with?

52
00:05:39,902 --> 00:05:40,945
‎No.

53
00:05:41,028 --> 00:05:41,863
‎Thank you.

54
00:06:00,673 --> 00:06:02,758
‎This is the final round
‎of the competition.

55
00:06:02,842 --> 00:06:05,178
‎Next up is Conductor Luca Domenico.

56
00:07:11,327 --> 00:07:12,286
‎Jeong-yo.

57
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:14,205
‎It's definitely Jeong-yo.

58
00:07:14,956 --> 00:07:16,666
‎But why did he say he doesn't know me?

59
00:07:20,836 --> 00:07:22,380
‎Today's winner,

60
00:07:22,463 --> 00:07:23,714
‎Luca Domenico.

61
00:07:38,354 --> 00:07:39,230
‎Mr. Domenico.

62
00:07:39,814 --> 00:07:41,691
‎Congratulations on
‎winning the competition.

63
00:07:42,608 --> 00:07:46,195
‎Recent accusations state
‎you are actually pianist Jeong-yo Choi,

64
00:07:46,279 --> 00:07:48,281
‎who disappeared nine years ago.

65
00:07:48,364 --> 00:07:49,365
‎What do you say to that?

66
00:07:52,577 --> 00:07:56,080
‎I'm so sorry,
‎but I came here to make music.

67
00:07:56,163 --> 00:07:59,667
‎I would appreciate it
‎if you didn't ask personal questions.

68
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:02,336
‎Are you admitting
‎that you're Jeong-yo Choi?

69
00:08:02,837 --> 00:08:03,921
‎As I said,

70
00:08:04,005 --> 00:08:08,092
‎I do not wish for my music
‎to be overshadowed by my past.

71
00:08:08,634 --> 00:08:11,679
‎Please limit your questions to music.
‎Thank you.

72
00:08:11,762 --> 00:08:12,805
‎Please answer us.

73
00:08:12,888 --> 00:08:15,099
‎What were you doing all this time?

74
00:08:15,683 --> 00:08:17,351
‎As the winner has requested,

75
00:08:17,435 --> 00:08:19,937
‎please refrain from
‎asking personal questions.

76
00:08:20,021 --> 00:08:22,607
‎Further details will be
‎provided later to the press.

77
00:08:22,690 --> 00:08:23,608
‎Thank you.

78
00:08:27,445 --> 00:08:29,614
‎Why were you gone for nine years?

79
00:08:29,697 --> 00:08:30,823
‎Why now?

80
00:08:41,834 --> 00:08:44,378
‎Oh my god, is that Pi-o Kang?

81
00:08:45,504 --> 00:08:46,422
‎I don't…

82
00:09:03,522 --> 00:09:06,442
‎I'm sorry, but Mr. Domenico says
‎he doesn't know you.

83
00:09:06,525 --> 00:09:08,110
‎He said he doesn't know me?

84
00:09:08,194 --> 00:09:09,737
‎As I said,

85
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:13,783
‎I do not wish for my music
‎to be overshadowed by my past.

86
00:09:14,325 --> 00:09:17,036
‎Please limit your questions to music.
‎Thank you.

87
00:09:24,085 --> 00:09:26,462
‎Prague police have warned
‎that pickpocketing incidents

88
00:09:26,545 --> 00:09:28,673
‎targeting tourists
‎have recently increased,

89
00:09:28,756 --> 00:09:31,967
‎urging both residents and visitors
‎to remain vigilant.

90
00:09:32,051 --> 00:09:33,177
‎Authorities stated that…

91
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:36,097
‎MISSED CALLS
‎JAE-IN

92
00:09:36,681 --> 00:09:39,600
‎…and that crime prevention campaigns
‎would be strengthened.

93
00:09:39,684 --> 00:09:41,811
‎In other news, Prague police are expanding

94
00:09:41,894 --> 00:09:44,980
‎their investigation
‎into a recent rise in vehicle thefts,

95
00:09:45,064 --> 00:09:47,358
‎particularly around
‎residential areas in the city.

96
00:09:47,441 --> 00:09:50,069
‎Yesterday, Choi Jeong-yo participated

97
00:09:50,152 --> 00:09:52,780
‎in a conducting competition
‎in Brno, Czech Republic,

98
00:09:52,863 --> 00:09:56,575
‎nine years after he went missing
‎during the Harmonie Competition,

99
00:09:56,659 --> 00:09:58,703
‎sparking a major sensation.

100
00:09:58,786 --> 00:10:02,957
‎Choi drew international attention
‎when he mysteriously vanished

101
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:06,377
‎during the competition nine years ago.

102
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:09,255
‎At the time, police confirmed
‎the committee received threatening calls…

103
00:10:09,338 --> 00:10:10,214
‎Pi-o.

104
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:12,466
‎Where are you?

105
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:14,635
‎Oh, I'm just…

106
00:10:14,719 --> 00:10:16,721
‎Have you seen the news?

107
00:10:17,388 --> 00:10:19,265
‎About Jeong-yo reappearing?

108
00:10:19,348 --> 00:10:22,476
‎Why did you change your name
‎from Jeong-yo Choi to Luca Domenico?

109
00:10:23,352 --> 00:10:24,687
‎The truth is…

110
00:10:25,312 --> 00:10:27,189
‎"CHOI" CONDUCTS IN THE CZECH REPUBLIC

111
00:10:27,273 --> 00:10:29,525
‎…I lost my memories from nine years ago

112
00:10:30,651 --> 00:10:32,236
‎due to an accident.

113
00:10:33,195 --> 00:10:35,698
‎Nine years ago
‎at the Harmonie Competition,

114
00:10:35,781 --> 00:10:38,576
‎are you the one who abducted this man?

115
00:10:38,659 --> 00:10:40,077
‎Yes, dead.

116
00:10:41,954 --> 00:10:44,540
‎Are you saying
‎you're suffering from amnesia?

117
00:10:46,834 --> 00:10:47,752
‎Yes.

118
00:10:50,921 --> 00:10:52,256
‎Are you watching the news?

119
00:10:53,632 --> 00:10:55,634
‎Pi-o, are you listening to me?

120
00:10:56,302 --> 00:10:59,180
‎Here is the budget execution status
‎for the second quarter.

121
00:10:59,263 --> 00:11:01,891
‎In terms of funding for performing arts,

122
00:11:01,974 --> 00:11:07,229
‎we have utilized about 78%
‎of the 41.2 billion won budget so far.

123
00:11:07,313 --> 00:11:11,150
‎BRNO COMPETITION WINNER, CHOI JEONG-YO'S
‎PAST CONTINUES TO SURFACE, CAUSING A STIR…

124
00:11:15,321 --> 00:11:16,155
‎Ms. Kang?

125
00:11:20,117 --> 00:11:21,035
‎I'm sorry.

126
00:11:22,161 --> 00:11:23,913
‎Where were we?

127
00:11:23,996 --> 00:11:27,208
‎I asked for your opinion
‎regarding the speech and the guest list

128
00:11:27,291 --> 00:11:28,959
‎for the Grand Prize of Lucena.

129
00:11:29,043 --> 00:11:30,669
‎Oh, yes.

130
00:11:31,879 --> 00:11:32,713
‎I'm sorry.

131
00:11:34,173 --> 00:11:36,258
‎I just got an urgent work-related message,

132
00:11:36,342 --> 00:11:37,718
‎so I got a bit distracted.

133
00:11:37,801 --> 00:11:40,262
‎Do you mind if we take a quick break?

134
00:11:41,096 --> 00:11:42,681
‎I need to reply to this right away.

135
00:11:43,599 --> 00:11:44,517
‎I'm sorry.

136
00:11:45,684 --> 00:11:47,770
‎Then let's take a break before continuing.

137
00:12:01,659 --> 00:12:04,286
‎CHOI JEONG-YO'S SHOCKING REVELATIONS
‎FROM DISAPPEARANCE TO AMNESIA

138
00:12:28,561 --> 00:12:31,188
‎"CHOI JEONG-YO" SEARCH RESULTS

139
00:12:52,001 --> 00:12:53,919
‎Please, let me see him.

140
00:12:54,003 --> 00:12:55,629
‎I'm sorry, Mr. Domenico has made it clear

141
00:12:55,713 --> 00:13:00,175
‎he doesn't want any personal meetings
‎other than agencies and music magazines.

142
00:13:00,259 --> 00:13:01,385
‎Oh, Pianist Kang!

143
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,346
‎Oh, how are you, Director?

144
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:05,681
‎I'm good.

145
00:13:05,764 --> 00:13:08,434
‎I absolutely loved
‎your performance last year.

146
00:13:08,517 --> 00:13:10,227
‎What brings you here today?

147
00:13:10,311 --> 00:13:12,646
‎I'm here to meet Jeong-yo Choi.

148
00:13:13,272 --> 00:13:14,106
‎I see.

149
00:13:14,189 --> 00:13:16,275
‎I won't take much of his time.

150
00:13:16,358 --> 00:13:17,818
‎Just a brief meeting.

151
00:13:18,611 --> 00:13:19,570
‎Just a moment.

152
00:13:19,653 --> 00:13:20,571
‎Okay.

153
00:13:33,167 --> 00:13:34,543
‎-Follow me.
‎-Thank you.

154
00:14:06,742 --> 00:14:09,244
‎Hi, it's nice to meet you.

155
00:14:12,373 --> 00:14:13,540
‎What are you doing?

156
00:14:19,004 --> 00:14:19,963
‎I'm sorry.

157
00:14:20,047 --> 00:14:21,799
‎I must've caught you off guard,

158
00:14:23,217 --> 00:14:24,218
‎showing up unannounced.

159
00:14:29,431 --> 00:14:30,808
‎You probably don't remember,

160
00:14:31,558 --> 00:14:33,560
‎but we went to
‎Korea Arts High School together.

161
00:14:34,728 --> 00:14:36,105
‎I'm Kang Pi-o.

162
00:14:41,694 --> 00:14:42,778
‎You can speak casually.

163
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,446
‎I'm fine with whatever.

164
00:14:46,115 --> 00:14:47,282
‎Okay.

165
00:14:49,368 --> 00:14:51,370
‎I thought you were dead.

166
00:14:54,081 --> 00:14:55,457
‎I'm so thankful…

167
00:14:57,918 --> 00:14:59,169
‎that you made it back alive.

168
00:14:59,878 --> 00:15:01,547
‎Why are you thankful for that?

169
00:15:02,047 --> 00:15:03,007
‎Well…

170
00:15:05,009 --> 00:15:06,552
‎because you were my friend…

171
00:15:09,054 --> 00:15:11,598
‎and I prayed for you to be alive.

172
00:15:15,394 --> 00:15:16,437
‎By the way,

173
00:15:17,104 --> 00:15:19,732
‎how did you lose your memory?

174
00:15:20,357 --> 00:15:21,900
‎Do I need to answer that?

175
00:15:21,984 --> 00:15:24,528
‎No, you don't have to.

176
00:15:27,865 --> 00:15:32,369
‎So why are you conducting
‎instead of playing the piano?

177
00:15:33,537 --> 00:15:36,874
‎I mean, your conducting
‎is wonderful and moving.

178
00:15:36,957 --> 00:15:39,043
‎But you loved playing the piano,

179
00:15:39,126 --> 00:15:41,170
‎so I was wondering if you quit entirely.

180
00:15:41,837 --> 00:15:43,672
‎You're going to play again, right?

181
00:15:43,756 --> 00:15:46,008
‎Why are you asking me that?

182
00:15:46,925 --> 00:15:47,760
‎What?

183
00:15:47,843 --> 00:15:50,512
‎If that's all you came to ask,
‎please leave.

184
00:15:56,852 --> 00:15:59,271
‎From now on,
‎please don't allow any personal visits.

185
00:15:59,354 --> 00:16:01,732
‎I thought I made myself clear.

186
00:16:11,241 --> 00:16:13,577
‎Anyway, thank you for coming back.

187
00:16:14,578 --> 00:16:17,581
‎If you ever come to Korea, give me a call.

188
00:16:21,376 --> 00:16:22,878
‎Can I give you a hug?

189
00:16:23,587 --> 00:16:24,421
‎No.

190
00:17:12,553 --> 00:17:13,637
‎Yes, Mr. Kang?

191
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:15,222
‎Have you arrived?

192
00:17:15,305 --> 00:17:17,724
‎Yes, I just arrived.

193
00:17:17,808 --> 00:17:21,228
‎So, have you thought of a way?

194
00:17:22,771 --> 00:17:23,814
‎Based on the articles,

195
00:17:23,897 --> 00:17:26,692
‎if we push too hard right away,
‎it might backfire.

196
00:17:27,276 --> 00:17:31,488
‎I think the best approach is to assure him
‎he can pursue the music he wants.

197
00:17:31,572 --> 00:17:32,656
‎And the orchestra members?

198
00:17:33,157 --> 00:17:35,617
‎I think they'll at least be intrigued.

199
00:17:36,118 --> 00:17:39,454
‎He's back after almost ten years,
‎and his talent speaks for itself.

200
00:17:39,538 --> 00:17:40,372
‎That said,

201
00:17:40,956 --> 00:17:43,208
‎we need to make sure
‎the process looks legitimate

202
00:17:43,292 --> 00:17:45,627
‎to prevent any talk
‎of preferential treatment.

203
00:17:45,711 --> 00:17:47,504
‎The concertmaster should be fine…

204
00:17:49,506 --> 00:17:52,551
‎but there might be pushback
‎from the cello section.

205
00:17:53,427 --> 00:17:54,761
‎You must keep a tight rein on things.

206
00:17:55,512 --> 00:17:56,346
‎I will.

207
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:59,224
‎Did you like his performance that much?

208
00:18:00,309 --> 00:18:01,935
‎Granted, he was very good.

209
00:18:03,145 --> 00:18:05,731
‎But you're still healthy.

210
00:18:05,814 --> 00:18:07,733
‎So why are you rushing--

211
00:18:07,816 --> 00:18:10,485
‎It's not about me liking him or not.

212
00:18:10,986 --> 00:18:14,156
‎When God bestows a talent,
‎it comes with a calling.

213
00:18:16,241 --> 00:18:19,786
‎Shouldn't we help him
‎make the most of that talent?

214
00:18:25,542 --> 00:18:28,503
‎The president of the Korean symphony,
‎Seon-ju Yoon, has arrived.

215
00:18:28,587 --> 00:18:29,630
‎Okay.

216
00:18:42,601 --> 00:18:44,770
‎Good afternoon, Mr. Domenico.

217
00:18:46,230 --> 00:18:47,147
‎I am

218
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:49,149
‎Seon-ju Yoon,

219
00:18:50,442 --> 00:18:52,110
‎president of the Korean symphony.

220
00:18:55,614 --> 00:18:56,865
‎Do you still remember…

221
00:18:59,326 --> 00:19:00,661
‎how to speak Korean?

222
00:19:06,917 --> 00:19:08,293
‎-You're here.
‎-Oh, hi.

223
00:19:09,169 --> 00:19:12,297
‎Where's Pi-o?

224
00:19:13,131 --> 00:19:14,383
‎He's in the practice room,

225
00:19:15,092 --> 00:19:17,719
‎but he still hasn't played a note.

226
00:19:41,159 --> 00:19:42,411
‎Are you okay now?

227
00:19:44,663 --> 00:19:46,081
‎You must've been shocked.

228
00:19:52,504 --> 00:19:55,632
‎It's such a relief though.

229
00:19:56,216 --> 00:19:58,593
‎We thought he was dead,

230
00:19:58,677 --> 00:20:00,262
‎but he came back alive.

231
00:20:01,513 --> 00:20:04,099
‎How was it meeting him?

232
00:20:04,766 --> 00:20:06,518
‎He wasn't happy to see me.

233
00:20:07,144 --> 00:20:08,729
‎I just said hello and left.

234
00:20:10,897 --> 00:20:11,732
‎I see.

235
00:20:13,567 --> 00:20:14,651
‎Well,

236
00:20:14,735 --> 00:20:17,446
‎it must've been awkward
‎having someone he doesn't remember

237
00:20:17,529 --> 00:20:19,281
‎acting familiar with him.

238
00:20:21,158 --> 00:20:24,953
‎Did you tell him
‎that you'd been searching for him?

239
00:20:27,789 --> 00:20:28,623
‎No.

240
00:20:28,707 --> 00:20:30,542
‎Why not?

241
00:20:30,625 --> 00:20:32,586
‎You're the only one who never gave up

242
00:20:33,086 --> 00:20:35,380
‎when everyone else forgot about him.

243
00:20:36,006 --> 00:20:37,174
‎You should've told him.

244
00:20:40,302 --> 00:20:41,303
‎In any case,

245
00:20:41,928 --> 00:20:43,930
‎everything turned out well.

246
00:20:44,598 --> 00:20:46,558
‎Jeong-yo is back safe and sound.

247
00:20:47,267 --> 00:20:50,354
‎Once he gets adjusted
‎and starts performing again,

248
00:20:51,188 --> 00:20:52,439
‎you'll be running into him.

249
00:20:58,862 --> 00:21:02,908
‎So when are you going to
‎start practicing again?

250
00:21:06,870 --> 00:21:09,414
‎Jeong-yo's back now.

251
00:21:09,498 --> 00:21:11,416
‎Maybe you should set your worries aside

252
00:21:11,917 --> 00:21:14,378
‎-and slowly start--
‎-Is that why you came?

253
00:21:14,961 --> 00:21:16,463
‎I'm just worried

254
00:21:17,672 --> 00:21:19,674
‎because you've been on hiatus for so long.

255
00:21:19,758 --> 00:21:21,510
‎I'll handle my own business.

256
00:21:21,593 --> 00:21:22,552
‎Do you…

257
00:21:24,096 --> 00:21:26,181
‎still need more time?

258
00:21:52,249 --> 00:21:53,166
‎Go already.

259
00:21:58,296 --> 00:22:01,341
‎KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

260
00:22:05,303 --> 00:22:07,806
‎I'm the king of the world!

261
00:22:49,556 --> 00:22:50,515
‎Hey, Jeong-yo.

262
00:22:51,766 --> 00:22:52,976
‎Let's be practice partners.

263
00:22:55,437 --> 00:22:56,521
‎What do you mean?

264
00:22:57,230 --> 00:22:59,524
‎You said you were too busy
‎preparing for the competition.

265
00:22:59,608 --> 00:23:00,901
‎No, I'm not entering.

266
00:23:01,818 --> 00:23:03,612
‎I want to be your practice partner

267
00:23:03,695 --> 00:23:06,406
‎and find a way to be happy making music.

268
00:23:07,115 --> 00:23:08,617
‎You'll help me, right?

269
00:23:39,314 --> 00:23:40,190
‎Jeong-yo?

270
00:23:44,152 --> 00:23:45,278
‎Kang Pi-o?

271
00:23:50,492 --> 00:23:52,160
‎You're Kang Pi-o, right?

272
00:23:52,953 --> 00:23:54,079
‎We met in Brno.

273
00:23:57,749 --> 00:23:58,583
‎Yeah.

274
00:24:01,628 --> 00:24:02,963
‎When did you come to Korea?

275
00:24:03,630 --> 00:24:06,633
‎It hasn't been long.
‎I'm here to discuss something for work.

276
00:24:08,802 --> 00:24:10,262
‎What brings you to school?

277
00:24:10,345 --> 00:24:14,266
‎I found online that I used to go here.

278
00:24:15,183 --> 00:24:16,142
‎So I stopped by,

279
00:24:17,060 --> 00:24:18,853
‎but I don't know where anything is.

280
00:24:24,276 --> 00:24:25,610
‎Are you just here to look around?

281
00:24:26,319 --> 00:24:27,487
‎Yeah.

282
00:24:29,447 --> 00:24:31,032
‎-So…
‎-You know…

283
00:24:32,993 --> 00:24:33,994
‎Go ahead.

284
00:24:34,077 --> 00:24:35,745
‎No, you first.

285
00:24:36,329 --> 00:24:37,455
‎Shall I then?

286
00:24:39,582 --> 00:24:40,750
‎I'm sorry about before.

287
00:24:42,252 --> 00:24:44,921
‎I felt extra defensive
‎around strangers at the time,

288
00:24:45,755 --> 00:24:47,632
‎and I was tired from the competition.

289
00:24:48,258 --> 00:24:49,134
‎I just…

290
00:24:49,926 --> 00:24:52,178
‎I behaved rather rudely toward you.

291
00:24:52,804 --> 00:24:53,638
‎I'm sorry.

292
00:24:55,265 --> 00:24:56,391
‎No, not at all.

293
00:24:56,474 --> 00:24:59,227
‎Someone you don't even remember
‎came by to grill you,

294
00:24:59,311 --> 00:25:00,895
‎so of course, you felt uncomfortable.

295
00:25:05,775 --> 00:25:07,444
‎Right, so…

296
00:25:10,238 --> 00:25:12,782
‎If you don't know where anything is,

297
00:25:12,866 --> 00:25:14,284
‎I can show you around.

298
00:25:22,250 --> 00:25:23,960
‎So what brings you to Korea?

299
00:25:25,170 --> 00:25:26,254
‎Oh, the thing is…

300
00:25:27,422 --> 00:25:30,300
‎I got an offer to be a guest conductor
‎for the Hankook Symphony Orchestra.

301
00:25:30,967 --> 00:25:31,926
‎Really?

302
00:25:32,469 --> 00:25:33,345
‎Yes.

303
00:25:36,598 --> 00:25:37,474
‎So…

304
00:25:38,725 --> 00:25:39,976
‎Are you going to accept?

305
00:25:41,686 --> 00:25:42,729
‎I don't know.

306
00:25:43,897 --> 00:25:45,315
‎I'm not sure yet.

307
00:25:46,024 --> 00:25:48,943
‎On one hand, it's my homeland,
‎so it might be better than elsewhere.

308
00:25:49,903 --> 00:25:51,821
‎On the other hand,
‎it might confuse me more.

309
00:25:53,365 --> 00:25:54,282
‎By the way…

310
00:25:57,202 --> 00:25:58,745
‎Were we close friends?

311
00:26:00,330 --> 00:26:02,582
‎We both entered the Harmonie Competition.

312
00:26:04,376 --> 00:26:06,419
‎Since you made such an effort to see me,

313
00:26:07,712 --> 00:26:10,048
‎I wondered if we had a special bond.

314
00:26:12,926 --> 00:26:13,885
‎Well…

315
00:26:15,387 --> 00:26:16,930
‎I thought we were close.

316
00:26:39,452 --> 00:26:41,663
‎This was our classroom.

317
00:26:42,247 --> 00:26:44,374
‎You transferred here during 10th grade

318
00:26:45,875 --> 00:26:47,210
‎as a gifted scholar.

319
00:26:59,973 --> 00:27:01,307
‎Where was my desk?

320
00:27:02,934 --> 00:27:03,810
‎Over there.

321
00:27:11,985 --> 00:27:13,736
‎And where was your desk?

322
00:27:16,322 --> 00:27:17,323
‎Right here.

323
00:27:22,996 --> 00:27:23,872
‎Yes!

324
00:27:27,834 --> 00:27:29,377
‎Do you remember anything?

325
00:27:30,670 --> 00:27:31,880
‎No.

326
00:27:31,963 --> 00:27:34,466
‎I guess I didn't
‎put much effort into school.

327
00:27:36,718 --> 00:27:38,595
‎No, not really.

328
00:27:39,262 --> 00:27:41,097
‎Then what did I put effort into?

329
00:27:51,733 --> 00:27:54,319
‎This is where we'd practice
‎playing four hands.

330
00:27:55,528 --> 00:27:58,072
‎You put the most effort
‎into playing the piano.

331
00:27:58,656 --> 00:28:00,700
‎Thanks to you,
‎this place and the practice room

332
00:28:00,783 --> 00:28:02,368
‎basically became my second home.

333
00:28:11,294 --> 00:28:12,795
‎What did we play?

334
00:28:14,047 --> 00:28:15,215
‎Can you play it?

335
00:28:36,653 --> 00:28:38,821
‎My tendinitis has flared up again,

336
00:28:39,447 --> 00:28:41,282
‎so playing has been a bit uncomfortable.

337
00:28:41,366 --> 00:28:42,575
‎You're in a slump.

338
00:28:44,452 --> 00:28:45,286
‎No, I'm not.

339
00:28:45,370 --> 00:28:47,163
‎How did you fall into a slump?

340
00:28:49,624 --> 00:28:50,959
‎I said I'm not in a slump.

341
00:29:24,409 --> 00:29:25,493
‎You asked me before

342
00:29:26,369 --> 00:29:28,621
‎why I'm conducting instead of playing.

343
00:29:29,998 --> 00:29:31,040
‎Nine years ago,

344
00:29:32,333 --> 00:29:34,419
‎I got shot in my right shoulder.

345
00:29:35,420 --> 00:29:36,629
‎It was not the plan.

346
00:29:37,213 --> 00:29:41,634
‎The plan was to let him go
‎after we got the money.

347
00:29:41,718 --> 00:29:42,802
‎But…

348
00:29:43,344 --> 00:29:45,722
‎he put up a bit too much of a fight.

349
00:29:45,805 --> 00:29:47,348
‎It caused nerve damage in my fingers.

350
00:29:47,432 --> 00:29:50,310
‎I can get through daily life,
‎but I can't play anymore.

351
00:29:51,728 --> 00:29:53,855
‎So I switched to conducting.

352
00:29:55,064 --> 00:29:57,066
‎But when I really want to play the piano,

353
00:29:58,735 --> 00:29:59,819
‎I play this piece

354
00:30:01,362 --> 00:30:02,906
‎and thank Brahms for it.

355
00:30:11,789 --> 00:30:14,083
‎I know how difficult it must be for you.

356
00:30:15,752 --> 00:30:18,129
‎Take away music from a musician,
‎and he's left with hell.

357
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:20,673
‎But a slump…

358
00:30:22,300 --> 00:30:24,135
‎is something you can work your way out of.

359
00:30:26,596 --> 00:30:27,597
‎That's not the case for me.

360
00:30:30,391 --> 00:30:32,352
‎I'm actually envious of you.

361
00:30:38,191 --> 00:30:39,692
‎Thank you for today.

362
00:30:42,153 --> 00:30:43,279
‎Let's meet again sometime.

363
00:30:48,660 --> 00:30:50,536
‎Okay. Take care.

364
00:30:51,788 --> 00:30:53,414
‎Let me know if you need any help.

365
00:31:06,010 --> 00:31:07,512
‎Nine years ago,

366
00:31:08,137 --> 00:31:10,056
‎I got shot in my right shoulder.

367
00:31:11,099 --> 00:31:12,725
‎It caused nerve damage in my fingers.

368
00:31:12,809 --> 00:31:15,436
‎I can get through daily life,
‎but I can't play anymore.

369
00:31:16,145 --> 00:31:17,313
‎Was it for money?

370
00:31:17,397 --> 00:31:19,565
‎Did you abduct him for that reason
‎or did someone--

371
00:31:19,649 --> 00:31:20,525
‎Enough.

372
00:31:20,608 --> 00:31:21,776
‎You want to know?

373
00:31:22,485 --> 00:31:23,903
‎Three million lei.

374
00:31:23,987 --> 00:31:25,279
‎Then I'll tell you.

375
00:31:26,197 --> 00:31:27,198
‎Where have you been?

376
00:31:32,286 --> 00:31:35,123
‎"You will again see the distinction
‎between the righteous and the wicked,

377
00:31:35,206 --> 00:31:39,002
‎between those who serve God
‎and those who do not."

378
00:31:40,628 --> 00:31:41,546
‎"'For behold,

379
00:31:42,588 --> 00:31:44,507
‎the day is coming, burning like an oven."

380
00:31:46,175 --> 00:31:48,219
‎"Says the Lord of hosts,

381
00:31:49,846 --> 00:31:52,640
‎'Not a root or a branch…

382
00:31:54,267 --> 00:31:55,685
‎will be left to them.'"

383
00:31:58,521 --> 00:31:59,439
‎Hello, ma'am.

384
00:32:00,440 --> 00:32:02,525
‎Are Pi-o and Father home?

385
00:32:02,608 --> 00:32:05,361
‎Mr. Kang hasn't arrived yet,
‎and Pi-o is in his room.

386
00:32:06,446 --> 00:32:08,281
‎Would you like me to prepare dinner?

387
00:32:08,364 --> 00:32:09,323
‎No, I'm not hungry.

388
00:32:21,085 --> 00:32:21,961
‎Pi-o.

389
00:32:24,881 --> 00:32:26,132
‎What are you doing here?

390
00:32:26,215 --> 00:32:28,051
‎Where have you been, Mom?

391
00:32:28,634 --> 00:32:29,510
‎I was at church.

392
00:32:30,762 --> 00:32:33,806
‎I was there volunteering as a lector.

393
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:38,811
‎Mom.

394
00:32:41,564 --> 00:32:42,398
‎Yes?

395
00:32:44,317 --> 00:32:45,234
‎Articles about Jeong-yo…

396
00:32:47,236 --> 00:32:48,488
‎You've read them too, right?

397
00:32:49,989 --> 00:32:50,823
‎Yes.

398
00:32:51,449 --> 00:32:53,159
‎Yes, I have.

399
00:32:53,743 --> 00:32:55,203
‎I was so surprised.

400
00:32:56,454 --> 00:32:58,247
‎I'm just relieved that he's alive.

401
00:33:01,793 --> 00:33:02,960
‎Are you going to see him?

402
00:33:04,629 --> 00:33:06,005
‎I already have.

403
00:33:07,423 --> 00:33:08,466
‎I see.

404
00:33:09,133 --> 00:33:09,967
‎So…

405
00:33:11,552 --> 00:33:14,305
‎Did he recognize you?

406
00:33:14,388 --> 00:33:15,681
‎No.

407
00:33:15,765 --> 00:33:17,100
‎He didn't recognize me.

408
00:33:17,183 --> 00:33:18,392
‎I see.

409
00:33:20,853 --> 00:33:22,855
‎I suppose life is full of surprises,

410
00:33:22,939 --> 00:33:24,899
‎but how could something like that happen?

411
00:33:25,691 --> 00:33:28,736
‎From the way he conducts,
‎it's clear he hasn't lost his touch.

412
00:33:30,029 --> 00:33:31,489
‎So at least there's a silver lining.

413
00:33:31,572 --> 00:33:33,032
‎"Silver lining"?

414
00:33:36,869 --> 00:33:38,454
‎Jeong-yo told me

415
00:33:39,038 --> 00:33:41,499
‎why he switched from playing
‎to conducting.

416
00:33:42,250 --> 00:33:43,292
‎Why did he?

417
00:33:43,376 --> 00:33:44,418
‎Nine years ago,

418
00:33:44,502 --> 00:33:47,421
‎he got shot in the shoulder
‎and lost use of his right hand.

419
00:33:48,798 --> 00:33:49,882
‎So I'm not sure…

420
00:33:51,759 --> 00:33:54,262
‎if that's really a silver lining.

421
00:33:58,808 --> 00:34:00,268
‎So that's what happened.

422
00:34:01,644 --> 00:34:05,189
‎But there are plenty of people
‎who switch from playing to conducting.

423
00:34:05,273 --> 00:34:06,941
‎Music transcends everything.

424
00:34:07,024 --> 00:34:10,027
‎As long as he's back to making music,
‎that's all that matters.

425
00:34:14,490 --> 00:34:16,701
‎Volunteering after a long break
‎really takes it out of you.

426
00:34:17,410 --> 00:34:18,369
‎Good night.

427
00:34:34,260 --> 00:34:36,345
‎MARTIN VOGEL

428
00:34:39,056 --> 00:34:40,766
‎CALLING MARTIN VOGEL

429
00:34:49,650 --> 00:34:51,068
‎Hey, Mr. Kang.

430
00:34:51,152 --> 00:34:53,070
‎How are you doing?

431
00:34:54,572 --> 00:34:58,034
‎If you're calling about Mr. Choi,
‎I don't have much to tell you.

432
00:34:58,910 --> 00:35:01,037
‎We heard the news of his death together.

433
00:35:01,120 --> 00:35:02,121
‎No.

434
00:35:03,289 --> 00:35:04,999
‎I'm not calling because of that.

435
00:35:06,584 --> 00:35:07,418
‎Then what is it?

436
00:35:08,169 --> 00:35:09,712
‎I have another request for you.

437
00:35:11,005 --> 00:35:12,048
‎What is it?

438
00:35:12,131 --> 00:35:13,216
‎Look into this quietly

439
00:35:14,425 --> 00:35:16,510
‎and make sure nothing leaks.

440
00:35:18,221 --> 00:35:20,056
‎I want to know who gave the order

441
00:35:21,682 --> 00:35:23,267
‎to abduct Jeong-yo.

442
00:35:34,737 --> 00:35:36,447
‎You haven't decided yet?

443
00:35:38,324 --> 00:35:39,158
‎No.

444
00:35:39,784 --> 00:35:40,826
‎Well…

445
00:35:41,994 --> 00:35:44,121
‎What's making you hesitate?

446
00:35:44,705 --> 00:35:45,706
‎You've already seen

447
00:35:46,916 --> 00:35:50,503
‎that our orchestra
‎holds its own against anyone.

448
00:35:50,586 --> 00:35:53,881
‎Plus, you'll get the authority
‎to appoint and dismiss members.

449
00:35:53,965 --> 00:35:55,383
‎There's no better offer.

450
00:35:56,425 --> 00:35:59,470
‎Isn't this the ideal stage
‎to pursue your music?

451
00:36:00,638 --> 00:36:01,514
‎I guess it is.

452
00:36:02,807 --> 00:36:03,641
‎Is it the pay?

453
00:36:04,517 --> 00:36:06,352
‎From our end,

454
00:36:06,435 --> 00:36:08,813
‎what we're offering
‎seems reasonable enough.

455
00:36:10,439 --> 00:36:12,024
‎Do you have a specific number in mind?

456
00:36:12,650 --> 00:36:15,319
‎No, it's not about money.

457
00:36:16,487 --> 00:36:17,655
‎Then what is it?

458
00:36:18,239 --> 00:36:19,824
‎What's holding you back?

459
00:36:22,493 --> 00:36:23,369
‎To be honest…

460
00:36:25,830 --> 00:36:29,750
‎I came because I wanted to meet
‎Maestro Kang Seung-woon.

461
00:36:32,253 --> 00:36:33,921
‎I have a favor to ask him.

462
00:36:34,797 --> 00:36:36,173
‎What is it? Tell me.

463
00:36:42,388 --> 00:36:44,765
‎You want to ask him yourself?

464
00:36:47,101 --> 00:36:50,021
‎All right, I'll arrange a meeting soon.

465
00:36:51,647 --> 00:36:52,481
‎Okay.

466
00:36:53,065 --> 00:36:56,110
‎By the way, you haven't signed
‎with an agency yet, right?

467
00:36:56,777 --> 00:37:00,740
‎I'd like to introduce you
‎to an agency I have in mind.

468
00:37:01,282 --> 00:37:02,658
‎Can I give them your number?

469
00:37:03,659 --> 00:37:04,702
‎What are they like?

470
00:37:24,930 --> 00:37:26,098
‎Jeong-yo.

471
00:37:27,850 --> 00:37:29,727
‎It's me, Hong Jae-in.

472
00:37:29,810 --> 00:37:30,853
‎Well?

473
00:37:32,730 --> 00:37:34,148
‎Does my face

474
00:37:34,231 --> 00:37:36,025
‎perhaps jog your memory?

475
00:37:36,108 --> 00:37:36,942
‎No.

476
00:37:39,320 --> 00:37:40,946
‎So you really do have amnesia.

477
00:37:45,284 --> 00:37:48,788
‎Still, it's a huge relief,
‎considering the alternatives.

478
00:37:48,871 --> 00:37:50,915
‎I thought you were dead.

479
00:37:51,415 --> 00:37:54,668
‎I was so shocked and sad
‎for the longest time.

480
00:37:57,421 --> 00:37:58,255
‎Right.

481
00:37:58,839 --> 00:37:59,673
‎Hey.

482
00:38:00,466 --> 00:38:02,468
‎We're friends, so drop the formality.

483
00:38:02,551 --> 00:38:04,095
‎I'm about to get upset.

484
00:38:06,514 --> 00:38:07,348
‎Here.

485
00:38:08,474 --> 00:38:12,019
‎This is the photo I told you about.

486
00:38:13,396 --> 00:38:14,605
‎Take a look at it.

487
00:38:14,688 --> 00:38:18,192
‎Can't you tell how close we were?

488
00:38:19,026 --> 00:38:19,902
‎Yes.

489
00:38:20,986 --> 00:38:22,321
‎It seems we were.

490
00:38:22,405 --> 00:38:23,406
‎That's right.

491
00:38:23,948 --> 00:38:26,700
‎You were a really special friend to us.

492
00:38:27,451 --> 00:38:32,498
‎That's why Pi-o refused to give up
‎and continued searching for you

493
00:38:33,207 --> 00:38:34,625
‎when you went missing.

494
00:38:35,668 --> 00:38:39,630
‎The only person who didn't forget
‎and kept looking for you

495
00:38:40,256 --> 00:38:41,549
‎was Pi-o.

496
00:38:44,427 --> 00:38:45,261
‎Why?

497
00:38:46,512 --> 00:38:47,596
‎Isn't it obvious?

498
00:38:48,597 --> 00:38:51,267
‎He was your closest friend.

499
00:38:52,893 --> 00:38:53,727
‎Actually,

500
00:38:55,062 --> 00:38:59,024
‎there's a reason why I wanted to see you.

501
00:39:35,519 --> 00:39:37,438
‎APPLICATION FOR APPROVAL
‎OF BUSINESS PLAN AMENDMENT

502
00:39:37,521 --> 00:39:39,064
‎NFCAPF STEERING COMMITTEE
‎KANG JI-HYE

503
00:39:39,148 --> 00:39:40,900
‎"Luca Domenico"?

504
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:53,579
‎Deputy Director.

505
00:39:54,788 --> 00:39:56,916
‎What is this application
‎for amendment approval?

506
00:39:56,999 --> 00:39:58,375
‎Oh, that.

507
00:39:58,459 --> 00:40:01,378
‎The Hankook Symphony wants to invite
‎the Brno competition winner,

508
00:40:01,462 --> 00:40:04,423
‎Choi Jeong-yo, as a guest conductor.

509
00:40:04,507 --> 00:40:05,424
‎Wait a minute.

510
00:40:05,925 --> 00:40:08,719
‎This isn't what we agreed to
‎when we approved the budget.

511
00:40:08,802 --> 00:40:11,597
‎They can't suddenly submit
‎an amendment request like this.

512
00:40:13,474 --> 00:40:14,642
‎The thing is,

513
00:40:14,725 --> 00:40:17,728
‎it's pretty customary to do this
‎for guest musicians.

514
00:40:18,687 --> 00:40:21,357
‎And Maestro Kang Seung-woon
‎strongly recommended him.

515
00:40:28,239 --> 00:40:29,156
‎Hello, ma'am.

516
00:40:46,882 --> 00:40:47,716
‎Father.

517
00:40:48,217 --> 00:40:49,260
‎Choi Jeong-yo.

518
00:40:50,052 --> 00:40:52,513
‎Did you suggest inviting him
‎to join the Hankook Symphony?

519
00:40:52,596 --> 00:40:53,931
‎Why do you ask?

520
00:40:54,515 --> 00:40:55,891
‎You know why.

521
00:40:55,975 --> 00:40:58,561
‎You never once gave Pi-o a second thought,

522
00:40:58,644 --> 00:41:00,729
‎but the second that bastard shows up…

523
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:03,482
‎Do you realize
‎how much this will hurt Pi-o?

524
00:41:04,066 --> 00:41:07,111
‎Why are you playing the victim again?

525
00:41:07,695 --> 00:41:10,489
‎How can you still be so immature
‎at your age?

526
00:41:11,073 --> 00:41:13,826
‎Why does it have to be him of all people?

527
00:41:13,909 --> 00:41:16,120
‎Pi-o suffered so much because of him!

528
00:41:18,038 --> 00:41:20,583
‎You're missing the bigger picture,
‎as always.

529
00:41:21,375 --> 00:41:24,503
‎Your son wasn't hurt back then.

530
00:41:24,587 --> 00:41:27,590
‎He grew the most thanks to Jeong-yo.

531
00:41:28,215 --> 00:41:29,800
‎That's why he won the competition.

532
00:41:30,926 --> 00:41:33,345
‎How can you work in cultural arts

533
00:41:33,429 --> 00:41:35,389
‎and have zero insight like that?

534
00:41:35,472 --> 00:41:38,392
‎Pi-o won the competition
‎on his own merits.

535
00:41:38,475 --> 00:41:41,312
‎Jeong-yo was nothing
‎but an obstacle in Pi-o's life.

536
00:41:42,021 --> 00:41:44,648
‎I won't let Pi-o get hurt like that again.

537
00:41:44,732 --> 00:41:45,649
‎Choi Jeong-yo?

538
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:47,818
‎Forget about asking him to join.

539
00:41:48,444 --> 00:41:50,029
‎Stop throwing a tantrum and get out.

540
00:41:50,112 --> 00:41:53,073
‎I don't have time to listen
‎to your petty complaints.

541
00:42:06,086 --> 00:42:09,131
‎Ma'am, Ms. Yoon
‎of the Hankook Symphony is here.

542
00:42:17,097 --> 00:42:19,308
‎Oh, you're here.

543
00:42:20,142 --> 00:42:22,019
‎You asked for me, Ms. Kang?

544
00:42:22,853 --> 00:42:25,064
‎I'm sorry for making you come
‎when you're so busy.

545
00:42:25,147 --> 00:42:28,150
‎You see, I have so much work to do

546
00:42:28,233 --> 00:42:29,610
‎that I can't step away.

547
00:42:29,693 --> 00:42:30,903
‎Please take a seat.

548
00:42:42,456 --> 00:42:44,458
‎I asked you here because I received a form

549
00:42:45,876 --> 00:42:48,671
‎saying you were appointing
‎another principal guest conductor.

550
00:42:49,380 --> 00:42:50,422
‎Would you mind…

551
00:42:51,924 --> 00:42:53,634
‎explaining the reason to me?

552
00:42:53,717 --> 00:42:56,512
‎Does that require an explanation?

553
00:42:58,097 --> 00:43:01,266
‎You know the conductor
‎we're looking to appoint.

554
00:43:01,350 --> 00:43:02,184
‎Right, Ms. Kang?

555
00:43:02,768 --> 00:43:03,769
‎Of course.

556
00:43:03,852 --> 00:43:05,229
‎How could I not know?

557
00:43:06,522 --> 00:43:08,732
‎I was so happy and thankful to hear

558
00:43:08,816 --> 00:43:11,485
‎that Jeong-yo came back alive.

559
00:43:12,653 --> 00:43:17,074
‎Then I don't have to waste my time
‎telling you about his star quality.

560
00:43:17,616 --> 00:43:20,953
‎His homecoming will be a much-needed boost
‎for the Korean classical music scene.

561
00:43:21,578 --> 00:43:23,789
‎Wouldn't you say
‎we deserve some praise for it?

562
00:43:24,456 --> 00:43:27,209
‎And what about the cost
‎of his star quality?

563
00:43:28,168 --> 00:43:29,294
‎It'll cost more.

564
00:43:30,379 --> 00:43:32,214
‎But if you insist on appointing him,

565
00:43:33,090 --> 00:43:36,552
‎we'll need to rethink your subsidy grant.

566
00:43:37,845 --> 00:43:39,096
‎Would you be okay with that?

567
00:43:43,600 --> 00:43:44,601
‎What is it about Jeong-yo

568
00:43:46,437 --> 00:43:47,813
‎that you dislike so much?

569
00:43:50,733 --> 00:43:52,234
‎What are you talking about?

570
00:43:52,735 --> 00:43:54,069
‎Who said I disliked him?

571
00:43:54,153 --> 00:43:56,989
‎Jeong-yo isn't even
‎Pi-o's competitor anymore.

572
00:43:58,073 --> 00:44:01,118
‎Is there another reason why you--

573
00:44:01,201 --> 00:44:02,661
‎Look here, Ms. Yoon.

574
00:44:04,955 --> 00:44:08,459
‎Are you implying
‎that I have no professional boundaries?

575
00:44:08,542 --> 00:44:09,835
‎My point is,

576
00:44:11,253 --> 00:44:13,714
‎chasing after stars like this

577
00:44:13,797 --> 00:44:17,885
‎does nothing for the development
‎of the classical music scene.

578
00:44:20,137 --> 00:44:21,054
‎I see.

579
00:44:22,681 --> 00:44:24,600
‎I understand now.

580
00:44:26,769 --> 00:44:27,686
‎But what can I do?

581
00:44:28,270 --> 00:44:30,898
‎I can't walk away
‎from a good business opportunity.

582
00:44:33,317 --> 00:44:34,359
‎It's disappointing…

583
00:44:36,528 --> 00:44:39,281
‎but we'll pass on the grant.

584
00:44:40,824 --> 00:44:44,077
‎I'm sure companies will line up
‎to sponsor Jeong-yo.

585
00:44:45,078 --> 00:44:47,873
‎As a businesswoman,
‎I can't let such a big catch get away.

586
00:44:49,374 --> 00:44:50,209
‎Please excuse me.

587
00:45:16,276 --> 00:45:17,110
‎Try it.

588
00:45:17,694 --> 00:45:20,989
‎I heard this place is super trendy,
‎so I stood in line to buy it.

589
00:45:27,704 --> 00:45:28,539
‎This is good.

590
00:45:28,622 --> 00:45:30,374
‎Right? Isn't it good?

591
00:45:35,170 --> 00:45:36,004
‎So good.

592
00:45:40,217 --> 00:45:41,760
‎Here, try this too.

593
00:45:45,889 --> 00:45:49,226
‎I got mad at how
‎the concert manager handled things

594
00:45:49,309 --> 00:45:50,352
‎and called them out.

595
00:45:51,520 --> 00:45:52,604
‎Guess what they said?

596
00:45:55,899 --> 00:45:57,484
‎Hey, Kang Pi-o.

597
00:45:59,236 --> 00:46:00,737
‎Are you listening to me?

598
00:46:02,739 --> 00:46:04,741
‎Yeah, I am.

599
00:46:04,825 --> 00:46:07,578
‎You weren't listening at all.

600
00:46:09,663 --> 00:46:12,416
‎Sorry. I'm a little tired today.

601
00:46:12,499 --> 00:46:13,417
‎It's okay.

602
00:46:14,042 --> 00:46:16,044
‎It wasn't important anyway.

603
00:46:17,588 --> 00:46:18,547
‎To be honest,

604
00:46:19,047 --> 00:46:22,259
‎there's something else
‎I really wanted to tell you.

605
00:46:24,052 --> 00:46:24,970
‎What is it?

606
00:46:26,054 --> 00:46:27,180
‎Did you know

607
00:46:27,889 --> 00:46:32,769
‎that Jeong-yo will be joining
‎the Hankook Symphony Orchestra?

608
00:46:33,937 --> 00:46:35,063
‎Oh, that.

609
00:46:36,064 --> 00:46:37,149
‎Did he decide to do it?

610
00:46:38,400 --> 00:46:39,443
‎You already knew?

611
00:46:41,486 --> 00:46:42,904
‎It looks like

612
00:46:42,988 --> 00:46:45,866
‎Mr. Kang specifically said
‎to bring him in.

613
00:46:46,617 --> 00:46:50,579
‎And Jeong-yo said he respected Mr. Kang
‎and wanted to collaborate with him.

614
00:46:53,123 --> 00:46:55,626
‎That's great. Good for him.

615
00:46:55,709 --> 00:46:57,169
‎Right?

616
00:46:57,252 --> 00:46:58,545
‎It's great, right?

617
00:46:59,379 --> 00:47:00,464
‎Yeah.

618
00:47:00,547 --> 00:47:01,715
‎Then how would you feel…

619
00:47:03,842 --> 00:47:05,302
‎about being the soloist

620
00:47:06,428 --> 00:47:08,764
‎for Jeong-yo's debut performance?

621
00:47:10,766 --> 00:47:11,808
‎What are you talking about?

622
00:47:11,892 --> 00:47:12,851
‎I mean,

623
00:47:13,852 --> 00:47:17,356
‎he's going to do a concerto anyway.

624
00:47:17,439 --> 00:47:19,399
‎Since he'll need a soloist,

625
00:47:20,067 --> 00:47:22,819
‎I thought it might be nice
‎if you gave it a try.

626
00:47:23,737 --> 00:47:25,030
‎I don't want to.

627
00:47:25,113 --> 00:47:26,448
‎-Why not?
‎-I just don't.

628
00:47:27,824 --> 00:47:29,993
‎I don't want to
‎think about performing yet.

629
00:47:34,581 --> 00:47:36,458
‎Don't be like that.

630
00:47:37,334 --> 00:47:40,170
‎Just keep an open mind and think about it.

631
00:47:40,253 --> 00:47:41,963
‎When you think about it,

632
00:47:42,047 --> 00:47:45,592
‎you were the happiest
‎when you played the piano with Jeong-yo.

633
00:47:46,176 --> 00:47:47,761
‎If you perform with Jeong-yo,

634
00:47:47,844 --> 00:47:49,971
‎maybe you'll get out of your slump faster.

635
00:47:50,055 --> 00:47:52,683
‎Why do I need Jeong-yo's help
‎to get over that?

636
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:56,728
‎You think I'm too pathetic
‎to get out of a slump on my own?

637
00:47:57,646 --> 00:47:59,398
‎That's not what I meant.

638
00:47:59,481 --> 00:48:03,110
‎I just need a little time.

639
00:48:05,487 --> 00:48:07,489
‎Time to get back on track.

640
00:48:16,123 --> 00:48:17,124
‎Mr. Kang.

641
00:48:18,041 --> 00:48:19,292
‎Hi, Jae-in.

642
00:48:20,085 --> 00:48:21,795
‎Are you just getting in?

643
00:48:22,587 --> 00:48:26,049
‎I'm here to talk to Pi-o about something.

644
00:48:26,717 --> 00:48:28,385
‎I see. That's good.

645
00:48:29,928 --> 00:48:31,763
‎Come inside and have a cup of tea.

646
00:48:31,847 --> 00:48:32,681
‎Pardon?

647
00:48:37,144 --> 00:48:38,061
‎We meet again.

648
00:48:39,604 --> 00:48:42,441
‎I had no idea you were his grandson.

649
00:48:43,150 --> 00:48:44,609
‎I hear you're joining
‎the Hankook Symphony.

650
00:48:45,694 --> 00:48:46,611
‎That's good.

651
00:48:47,821 --> 00:48:48,989
‎Let's talk inside.

652
00:48:56,955 --> 00:48:59,416
‎Jeong-yo isn't even
‎Pi-o's competitor anymore.

653
00:48:59,916 --> 00:49:03,378
‎Is there another reason why you…

654
00:49:05,756 --> 00:49:07,340
‎I need to find a way.

655
00:49:08,550 --> 00:49:09,551
‎There must be a way.

656
00:49:39,873 --> 00:49:41,583
‎Times have changed, Mr. Kang.

657
00:49:42,083 --> 00:49:43,960
‎There are more ways to market things now.

658
00:49:44,461 --> 00:49:48,215
‎There are lots of young people
‎who are wild about classical music.

659
00:49:48,799 --> 00:49:50,717
‎If we just use social media effectively,

660
00:49:51,551 --> 00:49:56,306
‎we won't have to rely solely on TV
‎or magazines to hype up the festival.

661
00:50:04,397 --> 00:50:05,273
‎Hello, Ms. Kang.

662
00:50:12,823 --> 00:50:14,616
‎I came to talk to Pi-o,

663
00:50:14,699 --> 00:50:18,370
‎then Mr. Kang asked me to stay for tea.

664
00:50:18,870 --> 00:50:19,913
‎Is that so?

665
00:50:24,501 --> 00:50:25,502
‎Jeong-yo.

666
00:50:28,672 --> 00:50:29,673
‎Do you remember me?

667
00:50:30,757 --> 00:50:31,925
‎I'm Pi-o's mom.

668
00:50:35,720 --> 00:50:37,472
‎No, I'm sorry.

669
00:50:38,223 --> 00:50:40,767
‎It's okay. I heard what happened.

670
00:50:42,686 --> 00:50:44,354
‎I'm glad you look so well.

671
00:50:45,272 --> 00:50:47,858
‎Don't just stand there.
‎Either go upstairs or sit down.

672
00:50:48,316 --> 00:50:50,527
‎Don't make my guests uncomfortable.

673
00:51:03,999 --> 00:51:07,544
‎I'm so grateful to see you again.

674
00:51:10,589 --> 00:51:12,674
‎You must've gone through so much.

675
00:51:13,508 --> 00:51:17,387
‎Do you mind if I ask
‎how you lost your memory?

676
00:51:18,388 --> 00:51:20,056
‎Oh, I…

677
00:51:21,391 --> 00:51:23,602
‎When I came to, I was at a monastery.

678
00:51:24,644 --> 00:51:26,897
‎I refused to go to a hospital,

679
00:51:26,980 --> 00:51:29,566
‎so I was treated by a monk
‎who used to be a doctor.

680
00:51:31,568 --> 00:51:32,444
‎When I woke up,

681
00:51:33,612 --> 00:51:36,781
‎I had no memory of what happened,
‎maybe due to the shock of surgery.

682
00:51:37,741 --> 00:51:39,784
‎Oh dear. So that's what happened.

683
00:51:41,703 --> 00:51:45,165
‎Yet you didn't give up
‎and continued to study music.

684
00:51:45,248 --> 00:51:46,166
‎I'm impressed.

685
00:51:51,713 --> 00:51:54,424
‎Do you still find it difficult to play?

686
00:51:59,387 --> 00:52:03,266
‎You still want to perform with him
‎despite his situation?

687
00:52:09,481 --> 00:52:10,690
‎Mr. Kang.

688
00:52:10,774 --> 00:52:14,277
‎Pi-o and Jeong-yo
‎haven't fully agreed to it yet,

689
00:52:14,361 --> 00:52:15,528
‎so that's rather…

690
00:52:15,612 --> 00:52:17,197
‎They can come to an agreement now.

691
00:52:19,741 --> 00:52:20,659
‎Pi-o.

692
00:52:21,242 --> 00:52:24,704
‎Jeong-yo wants to do a concerto with you
‎for his debut performance.

693
00:52:24,788 --> 00:52:26,122
‎What do you think?

694
00:52:32,837 --> 00:52:34,631
‎I don't think this will work.

695
00:52:34,714 --> 00:52:38,259
‎I'll recommend another soloist for you,
‎so give it another thought.

696
00:52:39,511 --> 00:52:40,845
‎Well…

697
00:52:40,929 --> 00:52:43,139
‎I want to perform with Kang Pi-o.

698
00:52:48,269 --> 00:52:51,231
‎He went out of his way
‎just to come see me.

699
00:52:51,815 --> 00:52:55,443
‎I don't want to choose another soloist
‎just because of a little slump.

700
00:52:56,236 --> 00:52:59,990
‎I want to follow Ms. Hong's suggestion
‎and perform with him.

701
00:53:02,575 --> 00:53:04,911
‎Pi-o, the truth is…

702
00:53:06,287 --> 00:53:07,163
‎What do you think?

703
00:53:08,456 --> 00:53:09,499
‎Are you against it?

704
00:53:10,250 --> 00:53:11,835
‎I think it'll be quite fun.

705
00:53:12,877 --> 00:53:14,212
‎Thanks for the offer,

706
00:53:15,672 --> 00:53:16,923
‎but I'm not interested.

707
00:53:22,429 --> 00:53:24,931
‎I'm sorry. Please excuse me.

708
00:53:38,445 --> 00:53:39,279
‎Pi-o.

709
00:53:41,990 --> 00:53:42,866
‎Pi-o!

710
00:53:43,950 --> 00:53:44,826
‎Wait a minute.

711
00:53:45,326 --> 00:53:46,244
‎Hold on.

712
00:53:47,579 --> 00:53:48,705
‎Hear me out before you go.

713
00:53:49,289 --> 00:53:50,290
‎Look, I…

714
00:53:52,167 --> 00:53:54,044
‎I'm really sorry for talking to Jeong-yo

715
00:53:54,127 --> 00:53:56,046
‎without asking your permission first.

716
00:53:56,129 --> 00:53:57,088
‎But the thing is,

717
00:53:57,714 --> 00:54:01,092
‎I wanted to gauge Jeong-yo's interest
‎before trying to persuade you.

718
00:54:01,176 --> 00:54:03,011
‎Why would you ask him first?

719
00:54:03,720 --> 00:54:05,305
‎You should've come to me first.

720
00:54:05,889 --> 00:54:09,684
‎That's because I had to
‎clear some things with Jeong-yo first…

721
00:54:11,978 --> 00:54:13,188
‎I'm sorry, Pi-o.

722
00:54:14,481 --> 00:54:16,524
‎I made a mistake. Just let it go and--

723
00:54:16,608 --> 00:54:17,942
‎That's enough for today.

724
00:54:18,860 --> 00:54:19,944
‎Let's talk later.

725
00:54:21,029 --> 00:54:21,946
‎Okay?

726
00:54:26,159 --> 00:54:27,202
‎Pi-o.

727
00:54:58,775 --> 00:55:01,444
‎I'm sorry for making a mess of things.

728
00:55:03,404 --> 00:55:06,282
‎I should've known this would happen.

729
00:55:07,367 --> 00:55:09,077
‎I didn't take it seriously enough.

730
00:55:09,953 --> 00:55:10,954
‎It's okay.

731
00:55:11,663 --> 00:55:13,289
‎I had a feeling he'd react that way.

732
00:55:14,874 --> 00:55:16,042
‎So…

733
00:55:16,126 --> 00:55:19,420
‎Does that mean
‎you still want to perform with Pi-o?

734
00:55:19,504 --> 00:55:20,797
‎Of course.

735
00:55:20,880 --> 00:55:22,298
‎I wouldn't have it any other way.

736
00:55:23,133 --> 00:55:25,260
‎Things just got a lot more interesting.

737
00:55:46,281 --> 00:55:47,699
‎I'll be in touch.

738
00:55:47,782 --> 00:55:48,950
‎Take care.

739
00:55:49,033 --> 00:55:50,577
‎And thanks for today.

740
00:55:51,327 --> 00:55:52,954
‎Okay. Drive home safely.

741
00:55:53,037 --> 00:55:53,872
‎Okay.

742
00:56:19,480 --> 00:56:20,440
‎Hey, bro.

743
00:56:21,691 --> 00:56:22,734
‎I just got done.

744
00:56:25,570 --> 00:56:26,404
‎Where?

745
00:56:27,822 --> 00:56:28,948
‎Oh, there?

746
00:56:29,490 --> 00:56:30,700
‎I remember.

747
00:56:31,784 --> 00:56:32,785
‎I'll be right there.

748
00:57:14,911 --> 00:57:16,329
‎CHOI JEONG-YO

749
00:57:18,790 --> 00:57:20,124
‎What was even more astonishing

750
00:57:20,208 --> 00:57:23,253
‎was your unique interpretation
‎of the set piece.

751
00:57:23,336 --> 00:57:26,464
‎How were you able to accomplish
‎such a difficult challenge?

752
00:57:26,548 --> 00:57:28,007
‎I couldn't interpret it.

753
00:57:28,091 --> 00:57:30,510
‎Even if I compete,
‎I'll just get eliminated.

754
00:57:31,844 --> 00:57:34,264
‎I've memorized everything.
‎Take it if you need it.

755
00:57:34,347 --> 00:57:38,226
‎I just focused on doing my best,
‎and it led to a good result.

756
00:57:38,810 --> 00:57:39,769
‎Come to think of it,

757
00:57:39,852 --> 00:57:42,230
‎you went to the same school
‎as that competitor, right?

758
00:57:42,313 --> 00:57:43,648
‎Were you close?

759
00:57:43,731 --> 00:57:45,191
‎I have to enter

760
00:57:45,275 --> 00:57:48,194
‎to help Pi-o get back on his feet.

761
00:57:48,278 --> 00:57:50,738
‎If he needs me to light a fire under him,

762
00:57:50,822 --> 00:57:52,782
‎I'll gladly do it.

763
00:57:54,409 --> 00:57:56,995
‎No. We weren't that close.

764
00:58:12,468 --> 00:58:13,303
‎Yes?

765
00:58:13,803 --> 00:58:15,430
‎Hello, Mr. Domenico?

766
00:58:15,513 --> 00:58:17,056
‎I'm so sorry to bother you,

767
00:58:17,140 --> 00:58:20,727
‎but there's someone here
‎who says he's your friend

768
00:58:20,810 --> 00:58:22,353
‎and that he would like to see you.

769
00:58:22,437 --> 00:58:23,313
‎A friend?

770
00:58:23,938 --> 00:58:24,772
‎Who?

771
00:58:25,398 --> 00:58:26,858
‎It's Pi-o Kang.

772
00:58:27,984 --> 00:58:29,152
‎Pi-o Kang?

773
00:58:29,736 --> 00:58:30,987
‎I don't know who that is.

774
00:58:38,411 --> 00:58:40,288
‎I'm so thankful…

775
00:58:40,872 --> 00:58:41,956
‎that you made it back alive.

776
00:58:42,040 --> 00:58:43,708
‎Why are you thankful for that?

777
00:58:43,791 --> 00:58:45,376
‎Because you were my friend

778
00:58:45,960 --> 00:58:48,004
‎and I prayed for you to be alive.

779
00:58:57,639 --> 00:59:00,516
‎SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK
‎FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

780
00:59:20,912 --> 00:59:23,039
‎FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

781
00:59:23,122 --> 00:59:24,666
‎Are you still afraid of going on stage,

782
00:59:24,749 --> 00:59:27,001
‎or are you uncomfortable
‎performing with me?

783
00:59:27,085 --> 00:59:30,004
‎By the way, what do you actually remember?

784
00:59:30,588 --> 00:59:32,632
‎Who was the man playing the piano?

785
00:59:32,715 --> 00:59:33,633
‎He was quite good.

786
00:59:33,716 --> 00:59:35,259
‎How about we perform together?

787
00:59:35,927 --> 00:59:38,304
‎Why are you pretending
‎to have amnesia anyway?

788
00:59:38,388 --> 00:59:41,182
‎Want me to break
‎a few of that bastard's fingers?

789
00:59:41,265 --> 00:59:42,642
‎What's the fun in that?

790
00:59:42,725 --> 00:59:45,061
‎You're really considering
‎performing with him?

791
00:59:45,645 --> 00:59:46,854
‎He's no good.

792
00:59:47,605 --> 00:59:49,065
‎Then do it with me.

793
00:59:51,567 --> 00:59:56,572
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

